{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>In that day. A vineyard of.</b> תירוש like תשתה חמר (Deuteronomy 32:14), and the meaning is that it gives much fruit:" "<b>Respond.</b> A song, like קול ענות (Exodus 32:18):" "<b>To her.</b> To Zion, and the word ענו refers to the musicians, and the prophet already mentioned above (Isaiah 5:7) that Judah is the planting of HaShem's delight:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:21.156022579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}